{"title":"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider five points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8859dbfb7a9ec734e16f2a88fb5cf1104eb6a39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c493dd2882ca1eb621281106a4d91bd73e092e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCED$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> be a line passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the interior of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and intersects \nline <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose also that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef75a70c8e27e5644c3cedb93824f38f69ecc358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=EG=EC$\" width=\"134\" height=\"12\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> is the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1fc15d59287d2ff7bf581a84f348b3207a0c64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4d6cd122415e7b7ccce4bdc0b15896ba36b846d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import cse5; import graph; import olympiad; dotfactor = 3; unitsize(1.5inch);  path circle = Circle(origin, 1); draw(circle);  pair D = (-sqrt(3)/2, -0.5), C = (sqrt(3)/2, -0.5); //G = bisectorpoint(C, B, D); pair Ee = rotate(38,C)*D; pair E = IP(C--Ee, circle,1); pair Gg = rotate(76,C)*D; path circle2 = Circle(E, length(C-E)); pair G = IP(C--Gg, circle2, 1); pair F = IP(C--D, circle2, 1); pair Bb = rotate(-104,C)*D; pair B = IP(C--Bb, circle, 1);  pair A = extension((-1,B.y),(1,B.y),G,F); draw(circle2, dashed); draw(A--G); draw(C--D--A--B); draw(G--B);  draw(E--F); draw(E--C); draw(E--G);  dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(30)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SW); dot(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, SE);  dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, SW); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, SW); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE);  draw(D--E,dashed); draw(B--E,dashed);  [/asy]\" width=\"385\" height=\"498\" /></center>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01fc0e485112d6e2a306370a45aa7d6b235b193e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAF}=\\angle{CGF}$\" width=\"136\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aef85bd32979e084348400b0c55af7090bc29af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAF}=\\angle{CFG}$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />, it suffices to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d832488ccc974a2d685f2be3d8985480c051a166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF=CG$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f3f03a121d03fdf26d1f93ee49c868c8f0d9b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FCE}=\\alpha$\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89d5de39148a5cef5ecd580b3b559fe022239f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{GCE}=\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c292fcd7c0c951a8c006e68d8ed24f8f5c9e5949.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CDE}=\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />. We have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/aff85c687abd60d1aaf0cad5a6264a587aeb52cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CF=2CE\\cos{\\alpha}, CG=2CE\\cos{\\beta}\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"16\" />\nso,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de10e236abb26e6bc8f0fd2e928c9a4720dfd41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{CF}{CG}=\\dfrac{\\cos{\\alpha}}{\\cos{\\beta}}\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"40\" />\nMeantime, using Law of Sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/41090650b60f3ae0013ce8d3ab4889e00ceffe45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{DEC}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, we have,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d27487e3917b3723f94aa581ec944ea428b61aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{CE}{\\sin{\\gamma}}=\\dfrac{DC}{\\sin{(180-\\alpha-\\gamma)}}=\\dfrac{DC}{\\sin{(\\alpha+\\gamma)}}\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"41\" />\nUsing Law of Sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d7b565c0c93de288a8452cb1b175b705911f909.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BEG}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, and notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7be5e235f54bacaf6e479e944e7e9fbc0d2fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CBE}=\\angle{CDE}=\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"172\" height=\"16\" />, we have,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/5/08568697090fd517f3b9f922d6a23186cf203434.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{CE}{\\sin{\\gamma}}=\\dfrac{BG}{\\sin{(180-\\beta-\\gamma)}}=\\dfrac{BG}{\\sin{(\\beta+\\gamma)}}\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"41\" />\nso,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc70eb8fc924fb7d38402f529c4599dc03228cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{DC}{BG}=\\dfrac{\\sin{(\\alpha+\\gamma)}}{\\sin{(\\beta+\\gamma)}}\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"43\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7636732a5f5a4f31b71e0ef4c6ad7c6a753b83a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{GFC} \\sim \\triangle{GAB}$\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/3/963ccf5da461b1e42d95a643157761ab0870ecb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=AB$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, we have, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14b79c23d391495cce2b55936cf04f65720512f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{DC}{BG}=\\dfrac{AB}{BG}=\\dfrac{CF}{CG}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"38\" />. Hence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/91639585ea48011a15cf5414e269ea60eaf66ad9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\sin{(\\alpha+\\gamma)}}{\\sin{(\\beta+\\gamma)}}=\\dfrac{\\cos{\\alpha}}{\\cos{\\beta}}\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"43\" />\nor,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/14208671a5027bca936b0b54bd4c1611a55a79e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{(\\alpha+\\gamma)}\\cos{\\beta}=\\sin{(\\beta+\\gamma)}\\cos{\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/85204f97b8216d17e155c7ff5245877d52427884.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{2}(\\sin{(\\alpha+\\gamma+\\beta)}-\\sin{(\\alpha+\\gamma-\\beta)})=\\dfrac{1}{2}(\\sin{(\\alpha+\\gamma+\\beta)}-\\sin{(\\beta+\\gamma-\\alpha)})\\]\" width=\"572\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04b0ed4a614daa9cfdecf7407d5100e521b1b45d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{(\\alpha+\\gamma-\\beta)}=\\sin{(\\beta+\\gamma-\\alpha)}\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"18\" />\nThere are two possibilities: (1) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c190c7f4033d5ea669793494eae99a0bbb025bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha+\\gamma-\\beta = \\beta+\\gamma-\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"179\" height=\"16\" />, or (2) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/3/0539118ef83c5c42798e03e20d468d3edc95c0ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha+\\gamma-\\beta = 180 - (\\beta+\\gamma-\\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />. However, (2) would mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5eec8f01def02448bc61b8d6231573163fc62d95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a771251838750a4cb9926c5e2b03324b2b2edae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> would be a diameter, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdcd63de18312ac11e62e75782e5158841d75bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF &lt; EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is inside the circle, so (2) is not valid. From condition (1), we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/911437c007caacf24d88e7a995dc2d1f5fe6c542.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha=\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d832488ccc974a2d685f2be3d8985480c051a166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF=CG$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Solution by Mathdummy\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO\" title=\"2007 IMO\">2007 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213733\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 200/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9103/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.064      1 -total\n 54.10%    6.527      1 Template:IMO_box\n 44.90%    5.417      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13385:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213733 and revision id 97368. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}